Diagnosed from a live session the user reported:
  F:\Work\demo2\asteroid-shamsu   session 20260822-090221-f144
  qwen3.5:9b-q4_K_M   Ollama 0.31.1


THE REPORT
----------
Two complaints, which turned out to be unrelated:

  1. "why wasn't the CLI UI updated?"  The rich renderer was plainly running -
     icons, timings, repeat collapse, reasoning blocks, panels, verdict badge -
     but the pinned input line and the telemetry toolbar never appeared, and
     startup said:

         Live console off (stdin is not a terminal) - turns render as a plain log.

  2. Two consecutive `/plan` runs wrote a plan file that said:

         ## Steps
         _No steps were produced._

     while the CLI printed, one line above it:

         Reasoning: { "title": "Fix Movement Math", "steps": [ { "description": ...


1. THE PLANNER — `think` unset is not `think: false`
-----------------------------------------------------
The plan JSON was never lost. It was in the `thinking` channel, and
`_generate` returns `text` and throws `thinking` away.

Confirmed from the user's own events.jsonl before touching anything -
`plan.planner_produced_no_steps` exists precisely so this is not guesswork:

    parse_error : planner returned an empty response
    top_keys    : []
    response_chars : 0            <- the response really was ""
    llm.thinking   : thinking_chars 1167, then 1068

Reproduced against the live model with the REAL PLAN_SCHEMA:

    think omitted -> response    0   thinking  624
    think: true   -> response    0   thinking  667
    think: false  -> response  561   thinking    0    (2 steps)

A `format` grammar constrains the `response` channel ONLY. Asked to think while
constrained, this model satisfies the schema INSIDE `thinking` and emits an
empty `response`. And omitting the flag is not neutral - the model's default is
to think - so "no think key" and "think: false" are different requests and only
the second one answers.

`_stream_completion` sent exactly the two shapes that fail and never the one
that works:

    if not want_think:
        return await self._stream_once(model, payload, ...)      # think omitted
    return await self._stream_once(model, {**payload, "think": True}, ...)

BLAST RADIUS. This is not a planner bug. `_generate` is the single path under
every `generate_structured` caller, so on the default tier's own anchor the
following were ALL returning "": planner, router, PRD development plan,
prd_headings, prd_entities, the strict repair proposer, the scaffold filler.
The 0-step plan is simply the only one that printed its own emptiness.

A second measurement, to place the boundary exactly:

    format=schema, think unset  -> response     0   thinking   155
    format=schema, think=False  -> response    22   thinking     0
    format="json",  think unset -> response     0   thinking  1611
    no format,      no think    -> response     6   thinking  1175

So unconstrained generation was fine all along, which is why chat worked and
only the structured paths were mute.

THE FIX — two parts
  a) Send the flag EXPLICITLY, both ways, and never ask for thinking on a
     schema-constrained call:

         reasoning = model_is_reasoning(model) and model not in _THINK_UNSUPPORTED
         if not reasoning:
             return ...(payload)                     # no channel to turn off
         want_think = wanted and payload.get("format") is None
         return ...({**payload, "think": want_think})

     A non-reasoning model is still sent nothing: it has no thinking channel,
     and `think` is not a key every build accepts. The existing 400/422 retry
     now covers `think: false` as well as `think: true`.

  b) A salvage net in `_generate`: schema requested, response empty, trace
     parses as JSON -> use the trace, and log
     `llm.structured_salvaged_from_thinking`. (a) makes this rare, but "rare"
     is per model and per Ollama build, and the failure it guards is total and
     silent. It is deliberately narrow - it never touches a call that answered,
     and it refuses `repair_json`'s "" / "{}" / "[]" so an honestly empty
     answer cannot become a fake empty plan.

VERIFIED end to end, the user's exact prompt through the real PlanningWorkflow
against the real model:

    title : Fix Movement Math and Rendering
    steps : 5
      1. Inspect input handling and velocity application in PlayerShip.js ...
      ...
    contains '_No steps were produced._': False


2. THE LIVE CONSOLE — the gate asked a question the library does not ask
------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if sys.stdin is None or not sys.stdin.isatty():
        _LIVE_CONSOLE_OFF_REASON = "stdin is not a terminal"

On Windows prompt_toolkit does not read `sys.stdin`. It reads the console input
buffer through the Win32 API. So `isatty()` can be False in a process where the
prompt works perfectly - and it was: the same session that announced "stdin is
not a terminal" then rendered box-drawing panels at true console width (rich
saw a terminal) and wrapped the prompt with continuation alignment
(prompt_toolkit was reading keys). Both libraries were fine. The gate was not
asking either of them.

The signature is stdin NOT a terminal while stdout IS one, which is what a
launcher that redirects only stdin produces. SHAMSU's own launcher does:

    $PipedInput = @($input)          # shamsu.ps1

Evaluating `$input` engages PowerShell's pipeline machinery whether or not
anything was piped. Measured while testing it: an interactive `@($input)` with
nothing to read blocked until the 2-minute kill.

FIXED, both halves:
  - The gate now asks the two libraries that have to do the work - can rich
    paint (`console.is_terminal`), and can prompt_toolkit attach
    (`create_input()` succeeding, and not handing back a *PipeInput). The
    reason string names which one refused.
  - `SHAMSU_LIVE_FEEDBACK=1` forces it on. The switch had only an off position,
    and detection being wrong once already is the argument for the other one.
  - The launcher only enumerates `$input` when `[Console]::IsInputRedirected`
    says something was actually piped. Fixed in `scripts/install.ps1` (the
    template) and in the installed `~/.shamsu/bin/shamsu.ps1`, so it takes
    effect without re-running the installer.

A TEST THAT GUARANTEED THE BUG
    test_the_off_reason_names_a_pipe patched `sys.stdin.isatty()` to False and
    asserted the reason was "stdin is not a terminal". It passed for exactly
    the reason the feature was broken. Repointed to what its name claims: a
    real pipe, detected the way the gate now detects one.


